      "reasons": [
        "The definition says “how prepared a person or group feels to take action,” but the packet only defines action readiness as the “degree to which faculty in a department feel they are able and willing to act,” without using or supporting the concept of “preparedness” or applying it to people/groups generally.",
        "The definition frames it broadly as “how prepared a person or group feels,” whereas the packet specifies it “refers specifically to faculty in a department” (and in context of equitable workload allocation)."
